+* ``_square_free`` removes repeated factors so every distinct root becomes a
+  simple root of a square-free polynomial (a repeated root is a common root of
+  the polynomial and its derivative).
+* ``_sturm_sequence`` builds Sturm's sequence of that square-free polynomial.
+  The number of sign changes in the sequence is a *rigorous* root count, so
+  roots are isolated without relying on sign changes of the polynomial value
+  (which vanish for even multiplicities and can be missed on a grid).
+* Isolated roots are then bisected using the Sturm count, which keeps all
